{"node": "spatialhistory", "row": {"person_id": "sherry_olson", "role": "historian", "context": "Places sampled and linked households (parish registers, censuses, taxrolls) on the streets and lots of nineteenth-century Montreal: mapped with GIS at McGill in the 1990s, then built with Robert Sweeny and others into the collective MAP geodatabase from 2000. The 2014 Canadian HGIS volume names MAP among the few Canadian HGIS projects since the 1990s; Sweeny, its co-director, questions GIS as a historical instrument.", "works": "“Le peuplement de Montréal” (1997); MAP, Montréal, l'avenir du passé (from 2000); with Dufaux, “Rebuilding a Neighbourhood of Montreal” (2014)", "source_ids": ["pe139_olson_peuplement_1997", "pe139_olson_dufaux_2014", "pe139_olson_bonnell_fortin_2014", "pe139_olson_sweeny_2009"], "basis": "source_review"}, "proposal_id": "pe139_olson_rel_01"}
