10-ABSTRACT/RESUME
11-The author suggests that Metis life was characterized by matriorganization.
12:Daughters were more likely than sons to remain in the West, marrying there and
13-contributing to the rapid population growth of the Metis. She proposes that
14-more detailed family histories could bring out important conclusions regarding
15-the development of Metis society in the nineteenth century.
