77-snowshoes, foraging, securing small game, etc., often came to be fully utilized
78-and much valued in both the HBC and Montreal fur trades. In the post setting,
79:Indian wives of traders often transmitted these skills to daughters of mixed
80-descent. The maintaining, in this way, of women's traditional productivity was
81-little respected or understood by the white women and other newcomers who
82-began to penetrate the northwest from the 1820's on. But again it raises
