95-Officer fathers who maintained these bonds often did so selectively, choosing
96-or being obliged financially to favour certain children to education and a
97-"civilized" upbringing. A sampling of these fathers, consisting of Nor'Westers
98:who had native children baptized in Montreal's St. Gabriel Street Presbyterian
99-Church between 1796 to 1821 (Brown, 1982), indicates that sons were selected
100:over daughters for such attentions by a margin of about two to one. The other
101:side of this picture is that daughters of these families were more likely by a
